{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790455326,"nonce":"70zKiBtPFMaxPlVEoxLDwtvo7WI=","title":"Zyntax languages have no machinery for their ecosystems' packages (pip, luarocks)","message":"A caribou project may carry a requirements.txt (Python) or *.rockspec files (Lua), or declare [dependencies.python] / [dependencies.lua] in its .cbproj. Caribou finds them (caribou_driver::deps::unresolved) but installs nothing and says so when a run starts, because Zyntax has no machinery for these ecosystems' packages yet (user, 2026-09-26). Needed from Zyntax first: a way to load a package installed by the ecosystem's own tool (pip --target, luarocks --tree) as modules of the language, including what its frontend can and cannot compile of a real package. Then caribou installs into target/deps/\u003clanguage\u003e and adds those modules, re-installing only when the manifests change (a first version of that was written on 2026-09-26 and set aside). Ask the zyntax session before planning.","files":null}]}